{"kind":"request","text":"Planner assigns the full design note and implementation plan from original8a13f7b, which authorizes own OR assign. Use a genuinely free design writer; do not preempt A4 or ready source reviews. Preserve the complete original brief below, including one unified live acts profile, ZERO durability, scope/content URI reuse, complete presence/messaging/third-example declarations and concrete implementation phases. Recheck actual local revisions and primary sources; distinguish current language from proposed extensions and explicit adoption decisions. Current definition.profile is rules-language selection, not a storage flag. Current Core one-item/sealed-entry/fact/receipt assumptions are real: do not call a memory Store swap an implementation, fake durable facts, or let a caller choose weaker persistence for a recorded act. Current authority/session/revocation windows remain explicit; no unrelated opaque-topic namespace or arbitrary external URI fetch. Retain observable generation/expected revisions/reset/bounded dedup, snapshot/watch handoff, fair coexistence and deliberate durable promotion with current authority. Irreversible effects require durable custody and are excluded from initial volatile profile. No physical scope combining or required persistent-state-only mode.\n\nDeliver exact dated design Source and plan, independent review and documentation landing. Runtime may be scheduled at a convenient time after concrete design/adoption; this request commissions ONLY design/plan, not immediate implementation or an unsafe weaker execution mode. Original requester may explicitly replace its to-planner bookkeeping with this authorized delegation, preserving every condition. No product suites or provider execution are needed to author the note; use static schema examples and focused proposed invariant witnesses.\n\nFULL ORIGINAL BRIEF:\nHugh's instruction, 2026-10-09: \"The URI should primarily be used to address a scope and its contents, which I think exists already. Please write a request for planner to publish a dated design note for this design, including the shared application definition language, and plan for implementation at any convenient time.\"\n\nPlease own or assign a dated repository design note AND a concrete implementation plan for a unified volatile acts layer alongside recorded Artroom acts. Suggested note: notes/2026-10-09-shared-language-volatile-acts.md (actual authoring date if later). Publish the reviewed note/plan through normal repository/workroom process. Schedule implementation at any convenient time according to planner judgment; this is not an urgent preemption of current work.\n\nACCEPTED DIRECTION\n- Hugh strongly agrees on shared application language and explicit guarantees.\n- COMBINE live signals/presence/messaging and live coordination acts into ONE live/volatile act profile. Do not expose separate live primitives or parallel signal and act APIs.\n- ZERO durability guarantee: the volatile state may reset at any time, including immediately after an applied response. Bounded retention/recent messages/idempotency aids are conveniences, not promises.\n- Initial application semantics approximately match Gitseq: (a) presence-at-URI for ephemeral coordination around attention; (b) messaging.\n- URI primarily addresses existing Artroom scopes and their contents (items, facts, proposals/versions, etc.). Inventory and reuse the existing address/reference/URI model; identify actual gaps. Do not default to an unrelated opaque chat-topic namespace or invent a competing URI grammar.\n- Shared syntax, type validation, actor/scope identity, authority/grants, guards, constraints, transitions, query/invocation/watch affordances. Different execution/commit/recovery guarantees must remain explicit.\n- Artroom already commits ordinary acts to DO SQLite before background external work. Git publication is separate and remains essential to actual Merged meaning. Deferred publication should not be mislabeled as reduced local durability.\n- Physical scope combining was discarded in the earlier architecture discussion; do not revive that option here.\n\nINITIAL APPLICATION DEFINITIONS\nPresence: an item owned by an authenticated SESSION associated with an actor; scope/content URI; present/absent state; attention status/focus and optional bounded note; runtime-managed lease expiration. Acts Enter, Renew, Set attention, Leave; timed Expire. Current queries select present items at a scope/content address; multiple actor sessions can project one actor's attention while retaining individual leases. Renew must preserve attention when omitted; explicit clear/update should have precise meaning. Don't equate one actor with one connection/tab/agent.\nMessaging: bounded message item owned/authored by authenticated actor/session, about an existing scope/content URI, optional conversation grouping, live reply reference, recipient actors and declared text/structured payload. Acts Say, Reply and optionally Acknowledge. Target attention to recipient active sessions without durable delivery/offline promises. Addressing controls notification priority, while read permission determines visibility; addressing alone is not confidentiality.\nMessages/presence are domain definitions built using the same items/acts/guards/effects/timed vocabulary, not mandatory built-in APIs for every future volatile application.\n\nTHE FULL NOTE SHOULD COVER\n1. Explicit guarantees/non-guarantees, goals/non-goals, and current-state/source audit. Applied means \"applied in generation G at revision N,\" never recorded/published. State and watches can reset at any time. No guaranteed history, broadcast delivery, offline inbox, timer execution across reset, external side-effect completion or durable exactly-once inference.\n2. Shared APPLICATION DEFINITION LANGUAGE in detail. Show complete proposed definitions for presence and messaging, plus one further small volatile coordination example demonstrating generality. Distinguish actual reusable current syntax from extensions; pin format/profile versions and validation rules. Existing definition.profile describes a rules-language profile: do not silently overload it as a storage flag without an adopted design. Determine whether execution profile belongs to types, act sets, state regions or scope instantiation; how live and recorded operations coexist within one logical scope; and how incompatible effects are statically rejected.\n3. Shared interpreter/runtime architecture: validation, current authority, guards, bounded deterministic judgments, expected revisions, local serialized application, memory store, observation. Identify which current Store/derive/applyEntry assumptions demand durable facts/entry construction and cannot just be disabled. Reuse evaluator concepts without producing fake durable FactRefs or letting caller request a weaker mode for a stronger act. Persistence/publication choices are properties of the declared operation, not an unrestricted caller ephemeral=true switch.\n4. Existing URI/reference integration: document canonical existing addressing forms for scopes and contents, resolution/incarnation/version semantics, equality/normalization, URI-scoped reads/watch/presence and routing. Distinguish stable addressed subject identity from a live generation/item ID. An address is not authority, and URI resolution must not mean fetching arbitrary external URLs. Handle deleted/inaccessible/superseded contents without leaking presence or misrouting replies. This correction supersedes the earlier suggestion that URIs primarily be arbitrary opaque topics.\n5. Authentication/session context: actor+session bound by trusted invocation context, never caller-supplied author. Session ownership versus actor ownership and multi-tab/multi-agent behavior; active-grant/read permissions, renewal/revocation, session capabilities and boundaries for independently signed acts. Define any missing session binding/operand and transport-independent API behavior for browser, agent/MCP and HTTP/RPC.\n6. Live generation, item/version/reference, ordering and duplicate semantics: current-generation local judgment order, latest-value/coalescing policies where declared, stale expected revisions, live reply references, temporary deduplication capacity/horizon, reset on mismatch, and possible unknown results after reset. Old IDs must never alias new-generation items. Zero durability does not justify accepting malformed/unauthorized transitions.\n7. Presence lease semantics: expiration enforced in reads/judgments even if timer late; cleanup/reclamation; Enter collisions and uniqueness by session/subject; explicit versus transport-assisted renewal; leave/disconnect behavior; delayed packets, actor aggregation and attention projection. Reset replaces any expectation of lease continuity. Describe bounds and no durable alarm required merely to clean volatile state.\n8. Messaging semantics: immutable author/subject/payload at acceptance, reply/conversation identity, recipient resolution and active-session notification, offline recipients, acknowledged/seen state, edits if supported, visibility/access, capacity/retention/reclamation, body/type limits. Specify whether overflow refuses, drops or coalesces for each declared type; do not silently evict data an acknowledgment promises.\n9. Query/invoke/watch contract: common discover-definition, invoke-act, read-items, watch-changes surface. Snapshot-to-stream handoff without missed intervening changes; composite observation retains live cursor/generation and durable frontier separately, not an invented atomic shared head. Reset/resnapshot/rejoin semantics. Transport backpressure, coalescing and targeted attention/inbox views.\n10. Live/recorded crossings: recorded-to-live reconstructable projections; live-to-recorded explicit snapshot capture and new authorized signed act with current checks and retained evidence; live-to-live best effort across scopes with generation/freshness/reset handling; recorded-to-recorded retains existing provenance/outbox/recovery. Signed live excerpts prove statements/context, not conversation completeness or their truth. No ephemeral references masquerading as durable foreign facts. If an external mutation is allowed, a persistent operation record must precede it; preferably exclude irreversible effects from the initial volatile profile.\n11. Resource/performance/lifecycle: high-rate live traffic must not starve durable turns; bounded memory, sessions, items, frames, bodies, fanout and catch-up; bounded guard/evaluation work. DO process eviction/hibernation wipes memory; connection attachments are a distinct optional lifetime, not persistent application history. Shared identity/permission checks remain even when storage/history costs vanish. Measure response/visible latency, allocations and fan-out before claiming improvements.\n12. Developer/person affordances: presence and messaging as initial declared applications under one live act API; consistent generated schemas/help, typed client results and verbs. Explicit Applied/Saved/Recorded/Published distinctions when relevant. Sample browser and agent/MCP flows addressing an existing issue/change/proposal URI, attention update, targeted message/reply, reset and deliberate durable promotion.\n13. Comparisons and architectural decisions: cite inspected local revisions and primary references for Gitseq, Terse, OpenInspect and PartyKit/PartyServer. Preserve distinctions between transient broadcast, persistent state snapshot, signed derivable history and external Git publication; don't borrow implicit method-interleaving or broadcast-as-commit guarantees. Describe alternatives/risks and identify adoption decisions/prerequisites rather than misrepresenting a storage adapter swap as full implementation.\n14. IMPLEMENTATION PLAN: bounded phases, exact source ownership/scope, dependency order, declared syntax/profile/compiler changes, volatile executor/session/generation support, presence and messaging definitions, shared client/query/watch integration, coexistence/promotion and acceptance. Planner may schedule/execute at any convenient time; no immediate urgency is requested. Identify actual decision blockers and resolve through existing owners. Plan focused meaningful invariants and one coordinated review gate per docs/testing.md, no mutation sweeps or blind repeated full suites.\n\nACCEPTANCE DESIGN SHOULD INCLUDE\nComplete valid/invalid declaration examples and common guards/constraints in both profiles; ownership and multi-session presence; forged author/session attempts; omitted vs cleared attention; leases and late timer; immediate reset after applied response; stale-generation references; dedup reset; transient message/reply notification and unavailable recipient; snapshot/watch handoff; role revocation; capacity/backpressure; live traffic fairness; same-scope coexistence; cross-scope reset/freshness; durable promotion of an exact snapshot while original live state moves/resets; no irreversible effect without durable custody. Prove recorded-act hashes/replay/authority semantics unchanged by adding volatile execution.\n\nINSPECTED FOUNDATIONS / SOURCES (recheck at actual design HEAD)\nArtroom packages/contract/src/definition.ts:18-43,62-103,170-238: items/acts/guards/effects/timed rules; current grant is mandatory. scope/turn.ts:335 and scope/core.ts:42 define durable sealing/receipts. lanes/change.ts:1642 marks Merged only for publication. Current live head streams in scope/sessions.ts are observations of durable state, not this proposed act profile.\nGitseq local HEAD c324aae7ce7bea6d0778e73efad1471d5db2c86d: host/live/live.go keeps signed generation-scoped frames and process-local leased presence; CompositeCursor at:219 separates durable and live progress. Shared signed schemas/opaque live payloads are relevant. Gitseq's addressed attention is not automatically a private conversation.\nTerse local HEAD924e5cd1ed87607e3e04e5eb29e20d335e733670: persisted/ephemeral declarations, versioned committed updates versus transient broadcasts; @Interleave changes rollback semantics, not a blanket safe latency optimization. https://github.com/TerseAI/durable-actors\nOpenInspect local HEAD8642fd42346840645db5b9f2afb60843c6445dce: ephemeral presence, durable session projections, canonical snapshot-to-stream handoff, separate sandbox/Git lifecycle. https://github.com/ColeMurray/background-agents ; docs/adr/0002-shared-session-contracts-and-correlation-boundary.md and0003-session-snapshot-handoff.md\nPartyKit local HEAD2faaaffcadec0856dcbcfd68d3b97e3f779be6e4: awareness/document persistence and explicit memory/storage/connection lifetimes. Current successor PartyServer, managed platform winding down. https://github.com/partykit/partykit/ ; https://github.com/cloudflare/partykit ; official migration guide apps/docs/src/content/docs/guides/migrate-to-partyserver.md\nCloudflare https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/concepts/durable-object-lifecycle/\n\nDeliver the published dated design note and concrete implementation plan, with current source facts versus proposed contracts, choices/open questions and planned ownership/sequence. Keep this unified live layer scoped to the accepted zero-durability semantics; additional persistent-state-only modes may be documented as future options, not made prerequisites for presence and messaging.","body":{"conditions":"Full dated detailed design plus bounded implementation plan; all14 original sections/address inventory/three full definitions/primary references/acceptance; independent designSource review and normal documentation landing","design_only":"true","implementation_schedule":"After independent design review/adoption at a convenient time; no preemption","priority":"Free design writer, alongside existing manual/N1; A4 and ready Source first","target_head":"9d7e4c2777ea8d35441b4a9d79b407cd701065fa","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}